<div class="help-wrapper">
    <h1>Welcome to the We Connect Dashboard!</h1>
    <h2>What is WeAre?</h2>
    <div class="items">
        <div class="item"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Afot8ypldsg">Origin of WeAre! Penn State</a></div>
        <div class="item"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D8591xRMIv8">Live of WeAre! Penn State</a></div>
    </div>
    

    


    <div class="ui segment">
        WeAre! is both a SlackBot and a community space for learners enrolled in PSU courses to engage with their peers
        and be part of the community. The WeAre! we propose here refers to a <a target='_blank'
            href="https://coil.psu.edu/blog/we-are-building-identity-participation-and-connectivity-within-world-campus-cohorts/">research
            project</a> aimed to connect
        learners across distance and build up their collective capacity as a community of learners. Thanks to the
        participation of numerous World Campus instructors and students, researchers from the College of Information
        Sciences and Technology at Penn State have found a lot about what a community of World Campus is for its
        members, using a mix of research methods, through a series of studies.
    </div>
    <h2>What is Slack team WeAre!</h2>
    <h4>What is Slack</h4>
    <div class="ui segment">
        Slack is a team messaging application, with an expanded ecosystem of intelligent bots to help make your
        cooperation and collaborations with others easier. In slack, users can sign in to their workspace (in the form
        of domain.slack.com) in various manners (e.g. Desktop, Mobile Devices, or Web Browser). You can create or join
        any channels (public, denoted by #) or groups (private, denoted by 🔒). Please refer to the following links for
        getting started with Slack.
    </div>
    <h4>How to use Slack?</h4>
    <a href="https://get.slack.help/hc/en-us">Official slack help center</a>
    <h4>How to use WeAre! bot?</h4>
    <div class="ui basic large  blue">There are three ways of using WeAre! in addition to the basic slack functions
        above.</div>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Onboarding/Self-intro <div class="subheader">/we-intro</div>
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Once you join the team and consent to the research participation, you will be welcomed with a
                    Slackbot WeAre! with the guide
                    to introduce yourself (e.g. fun fact, city, profession). Then you will have the opportunity to be
                    introduced by WeAre! to the team,
                    and received a lot of love and support from your Penn State peers here.<br><br>
                In the future, whenever you want to get some support, you could always introduce yourself by /intro
                    command in the text window and hit ENTER.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Study/Discuss with peers <div class="subheader">/we-discuss</div>
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Initiating discussion with other channel members now or later. After typing the command, you can initiate a new conversation via Hangout/1:1 call or to schedule a meeting with other channel members.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Who is online with me now <div class="subheader">/we-are-now</div>
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                See who is online now, and invite peers into a video session via Hangout call.
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <h2> What is WeConnect Dashboard?</h2>
    <div class="ui segment">
        The WeConnect dashboard visualize the Slack activities and peer information to help you find other peers based on your educational interests, and organize social activities. For example, you might wonder
        who is available with you now to ask a question, and you can find that availability information in others' profile view. In addition, you can also go to the "Peer Availability" tab under the Connect in the Navigtation Bar. 
        In the Availability view, you can easily see others peers' temporal availability based on their current online status, and their local time in different time zones.
    </div>
    <div class="ui basic blue large label">There are peers here visualized in the table view, or in the timezone distribution view. (More to come)</div>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Schedule and manage meetings 
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                You can manage the meeting invitations by accepting or rejecting them. You can also create your own meeting by either going to the channel 
                in which your meeting guests are in to schedule a meeting later (type in `we-discuss` and hit ENTER), or click the New Meeting button.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                Browse your peers' educational information in the table view
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Who is in common with me in terms of major, location and channel subscription in Slack. Shared attributes are colored.
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <div class="ui header">
                View others' availability in terms of current presence and timezones
            </div>
            <div class="ui content">
                Who is online with me based on Slack logging status and time zone.
            </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="ui label basic large teal">Feel free to post questions in the #help-slack channels if you have technical issues.</div>
